From: SiliconBedrock <siliconbedrock@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Keep the app bundle's icon on request.

With WINEMAC_KEEP_BUNDLE_ICON set, the driver doesn't replace the Dock icon with the executable's:
a Windows program started from an app bundle keeps that app's icon.

Original work for SiliconBedrock (LGPL-2.1-or-later).

Topic: bundle-icon
---
 dlls/winemac.drv/window.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
@@ -935,7 +935,12 @@ void activate_on_following_focus(void)
  */
 static void set_app_icon(void)
 {
-    CFArrayRef images = create_app_icon_images();
+    CFArrayRef images;
+
+    /* Keep the icon of the enclosing app bundle instead of the executable's. */
+    if (getenv("WINEMAC_KEEP_BUNDLE_ICON")) return;
+
+    images = create_app_icon_images();
     if (images)
     {
         macdrv_set_application_icon(images);
-- 
